Survey 3 is written to `runs/Absolute_2026-09-28_02/sota/cycle-001/survey-3.json`.

The pose callback poses one selected detection. Inference time is dominated by the bilinear chamfer grids in `coarse_chamfer_search_v2`: **28,306** free poses at the default steps, and about **17,386** more whenever the free cost is worse than about 6.2 mm, because the prior search then runs as well. Each of those evaluations copies the 182-point prototype and fully sorts it, even though only 90% of the distances are kept. Ahead of that, every pair scans the full 640×480 depth image, zero-fills a 1920×1080 mask, and builds an OpenCV precise distance image padded by 0.80 m. On the production launch, stage 1 is the TensorRT RT-DETRv2 R18 engine at 640, plus several full-frame host copies of the 1920×1080 RGB image.
